</figure>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Language Models.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A2.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ Inference Details and Parameters. ‣ Appendix B Additional Experimental Details ‣ Camellia : Benchmarking Cultural Biases in LLMs for Asian Languages" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> lists the LLMs used in our experiments with their HuggingFace repositories. We used the largest size available for each LLM family and included the most recent version that mentions multilingual support. We also restricted our experiments to open-sourced models since we can obtain their log-probabilities, which are essential to compute the CBS scores in our cultural context adaptation experiment (§<a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Cultural Context Adaptation ‣ 3 Are Cultural Biases Consistent Across Languages and LLMs? ‣ Camellia : Benchmarking Cultural Biases in LLMs for Asian Languages" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T6" class="ltx_table">
<div id="A2.T6.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:424.3pt;height:72.8pt;vertical-align:-33.9pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(0.0pt,0.0pt) scale(1,1) ;">
