<section id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Detailed Extractive QA Results.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Tables <a href="#A3.T10" title="Table 10 ‣ Detailed Extractive QA Results. ‣ C.3 Extractive QA ‣ Appendix C Additional Results ‣ Camellia : Benchmarking Cultural Biases in LLMs for Asian Languages" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> and <a href="#A3.T11" title="Table 11 ‣ Detailed Extractive QA Results. ‣ C.3 Extractive QA ‣ Appendix C Additional Results ‣ Camellia : Benchmarking Cultural Biases in LLMs for Asian Languages" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> show the detailed accuracy results on the extractive QA task. We compute accuracy based on the exact match of identifying the entity in the context. We observe large accuracy gaps between sets containing Asian and Western entities when testing in the respective Asian language of each culture, where LLMs mostly perform better at extracting Asian-associated entities. In contrast, these gaps are negligible in English in nearly all cases (2%-5% gaps). In a couple of cases, large gaps in English are observed (Pakistani vs Western entities in Llama and Qwen, Indian vs Western entities in Qwen).</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T10" class="ltx_table">
